 is \\(k\\).\n\n5. **Distinctness.**  \n   The slopes of the sunny lines are the distinct integers \\(1,2,\\dots ,k\\);\n   the vertical lines have undefined slope, so all \\(n\\) lines are distinct.\n\nThus for the chosen \\(k\\) we have produced \\(n\\) distinct lines satisfying the\ncovering condition and containing exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines.  \u220e\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Conclusion\n\nLemma\u202f1 shows that any admissible number of sunny lines must satisfy\n\\(0\\le k\\le n\\).  Lemma\u202f2 provides, for each integer in this interval, an\nexplicit configuration of \\(n\\) lines meeting all requirements.  Therefore the\nset of all possible values of \\(k\\) is precisely  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n\\}} .\n\\]"
